# `for (i) d[i] = q[i]; ... d[sel_q].field = x;` on an unpacked array of structs
# that ANOTHER process reads whole (`q <= d;`), so the array is MIXED: a flat
# alias assembled from the element wires.  The comb block owns per-ELEMENT
# temps, and the dynamic field write must read-modify-write those in-flight
# elements -- reading the flat alias (driven by this very process) closes a
# combinational loop (CVA6 trigger_module: tdata3_o followed tdata3_i with no
# clock edge).  `check -assert` after proc is the gate; `opt -fast` would hide
# the loop here because every field of the element is written.
read_uhdm slpp_all/surelog.uhdm
hierarchy -check -top dut
proc
opt_clean
check -assert
